 "response": "Tido's budget is now **$3930K**.\n\n**How I got there**\n- Only Finance Office budget entries count. Notes from PMO, Legal, Sales, Vendor, Facilities, Engineering, Marketing and Operations don't change the budget. Finance Office entries that aren't budget changes, such as receipts or audits, don't either.\n- The starting value is $1650K, set by #0001.\n- For each withdrawal, I traced the full chain. If a withdrawal was itself withdrawn, its target goes back into effect. Some examples:\n  - #0007 stays in effect: #0575 withdraws #0175, which reinstates #0031, which cancels #0011.\n  - #0004 is removed: #0121 cancels #0115, so #0014 stands.\n  - #0030 is removed: #0095 cancels #0073, so #0067 stands.\n  - #0028 is removed: #0955 \u2192 #0727 \u2192 #0361 \u2192 #0295 \u2192 #0093.\n  - #0041 stays in effect: the chain #0831 \u2192 #0268 \u2192 #0237 \u2192 #0145 \u2192 #0130 \u2192 #0120 ends with #0120 withdrawn.\n  - #0083 is removed: #1528 cancels #0792, so #0100 stands.\n- 105 budget updates end up withdrawn. Examples are #0002, #0018, #0088, #0181, #0248, #0430, #0443, #1146 and #1218. I applied every other Finance Office increase and decrease once, in record order.\n\nI did a single sequential pass and did not re-add the total independently.\n\nANSWER: $3930K",
